{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 9, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Raymond III Count of Tripoli also known as Raymond II of Antioch was a nobleman from the noble House of Poitiers born in 1140 in France he was the son of Raymond of Poitiers and Constance of Antioch. In 1153 Raymond's mother sent for him to come to Antioch to assume the title of Prince after his father's death. However upon his arrival he found that his mother had married another nobleman Bohemond III of Antioch.\n\n\nRaymond III Count of Tripoli had a contentious relationship with his stepfather and his mother. In 1156 Raymond was captured by the forces of Nur ad-Din the Zengid ruler of Aleppo and Damascus. Nur ad-Din released Raymond in 1158 in exchange for the city of Harem. Raymond then returned to Antioch and attempted to assert his authority over the principality. However, he was unsuccessful and was exiled by his stepfather.\n\n\n*Exile and Crusade*\n\nRaymond III Count of Tripoli spent the next few years in exile in the County of Tripoli. In 1164 he joined the forces of King Amalric I of Jerusalem on a crusade against Nur ad-Din. During the Battle of Harim Raymond was captured once again by the forces of Nur ad-Din. He remained in captivity until 1173 when he was released after promising to pay a ransom and to assist Nur ad-Din in his military campaigns.\n\n\n*Return to Power*\n\nRaymond III Count of Tripoli returned to the County of Tripoli in 1174 after the death of his uncle, Raymond II of Tripoli. He assumed the title of count and began to assert his authority over the county. Raymond III was known for his military prowess and his ability to defend the county against the forces of Nur ad-Din and Saladin the Ayyubid sultan. He also maintained good relations with the Byzantine Empire and the Republic of Genoa.\n\n\n*Death and Legacy*\n\nRaymond III Count of Tripoli died in 1187. His death marked the end of the House of Poitiers' rule over the County of Tripoli. Raymond III was succeeded by Bohemond IV of Antioch, the son of his stepfather, Bohemond III of Antioch. Raymond III is remembered for his military accomplishments and his ability to defend the County of Tripoli against its enemies. He is also remembered for his contentious relationship with his stepfather and his mother, and for his time spent in exile and captivity.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.00045372682507149875}, {"token": "III", "logprob": -0.00016473367577418685}, {"token": "Count", "logprob": -0.3620835840702057}, {"token": "of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "Tri", "logprob": -1.6689160474925302e-05}, {"token": "pol", "logprob": -7.152555099310121e-07}, {"token": "i", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "also", "logprob": -0.5624160170555115}, {"token": "known", "logprob": -0.006873534061014652}, {"token": "as", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -9.536697689327411e-06}, {"token": "II", "logprob": -0.7273396253585815}, {"token": "of", "logprob": -0.00012659224739763886}, {"token": "Ant", "logprob": -1.7620784044265747}, {"token": "io", "logprob": -0.0011961455456912518}, {"token": "ch", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "was", "logprob": -0.02183784544467926}, {"token": "a", "logprob": -0.3880445659160614}, {"token": "noble", "logprob": -0.2218054085969925}, {"token": "man", "logprob": -0.09946122020483017}, {"token": "from", "logprob": -0.7636176943778992}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -5.245195097813848e-06}, {"token": "noble", "logprob": -1.874258041381836}, {"token": "House", "logprob": -1.111703634262085}, {"token": "of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "Po", "logprob": -0.03375699743628502}, {"token": "it", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": "iers", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "born", "logprob": -4.428266525268555}, {"token": "in", "logprob": -0.0019024383509531617}, {"token": "", "logprob": -0.021415075287222862}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1",